implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST: create moe-vscode/tests/protected-daemon-spawn.test.cjs (node:test, run by `npm test`).

Harness, following tests/daemon-start.test.cjs and RF06's tests/protected-runtime.test.cjs:
- Transpile src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts into a vm context with:
  - real fs and path;
  - process = { ...process, env: <per-test env>, platform: process.platform };
  - a fake child_process.spawn that records [command, args, options] and returns an EventEmitter that emits 'spawn' on setImmediate, with unref() a no-op;
  - a fake vscode: window.showErrorMessage records messages, createOutputChannel collects log lines, and workspace.getConfiguration().get() returns its default argument.
- Build `new MoeDaemonClient(extDir)` and stub waitForDaemonInfo as async no-op.
- For protected cases, replace resolveGlobalConfigDaemonPath and resolveDaemonRuntime with functions that throw 'consulted'.
- Use fresh mkdtemp dirs and a fresh module load per test, so session pins never leak.
- Results from the vm realm (spawn args and options, protectedDaemonCommand objects) must be compared through JSON or spread: cross-realm deepStrictEqual fails (mem gotcha-vscode-vm-test-harnesses).

Cases:

D1. Setup: a verified-local project; extDir/bundled/daemon/index.js; a fake node file `node` (`node.exe` on win32) in an outside temp dir set as MOE_NODE_COMMAND; env with NODE_OPTIONS, NODE_PATH and PATH = [relative 'rel/bin', '<project>/bin', '<outsideDir>']. Call startDaemon('init', project). Expect exactly one spawn:
- command === realpath(node);
- args equal [realpath(daemon), 'start', '--project', project]. Under protected it is always 'start', with no --name, as in JetBrains;
- options.cwd === dirname(realpath(daemon));
- options.env has no NODE_OPTIONS and no NODE_PATH;
- options.env PATH entries are exactly [dirname(realpath(node)), '<outsideDir>'], followed only by bootstrap dirs that exist (none in the test, since HOME is an empty temp dir);
- no error is shown.

D2. bundled/daemon/index.js missing: no spawn. Errors deep-equal ['Protected execution profile: installed daemon/index.js not found. Project and PATH copies of the Moe daemon are not used.']. The global-config and resolveDaemonRuntime stubs are never called.

D3. With MOE_NODE_COMMAND='node' the refusal reason is 'node executable is not an absolute path'. With MOE_NODE_COMMAND=<file inside the project> it is 'node executable resolves inside the project'. No spawn in either case.

D4. No MOE_NODE_COMMAND, HOME an empty temp dir, PATH = ['<project>/bin' holding a node file, 'relbin', '<outside1>' without node, '<outside2>' holding a node file]: the spawn command === realpath(outside2 node). The project and relative entries are never searched.

D5. protectedNodeCandidate units, using windows=true, which is portable on Linux because the candidates are env-driven:
- with empty PATH and ProgramFiles set to a temp dir holding nodejs/node.exe, it returns that file;
- with nothing found it returns undefined, and protectedDaemonCommand(project, root, undefined) gives { refused: 'node executable not found' }.

D6. protectedDaemonEnvironment units:
- windows=true with keys 'Path', 'PATH', 'node_options', 'Node_Path': exactly one PATH spelling is kept (the sorted-first one, as JetBrains applyDaemonPath keeps it), both node keys are removed case-insensitively, and project/relative entries are dropped;
- windows=false: NODE_OPTIONS and NODE_PATH are removed and PATH is filtered.

D7. Legacy: a project with no .moe/project.json calls startDaemon('start') through today's path (the resolveDaemonRuntime stub is used). The spawn options object has exactly the keys detached, stdio, windowsHide and env, with no cwd.

Run `node --test tests/protected-daemon-spawn.test.cjs`: it must fail only on the missing behaviour.

In moe-vscode/src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts, extend RF06's exported 'Protected runtime selection' section. Add no new local import: five vm harnesses transpile this file alone. Mirror JetBrains MoeDaemonSupervisor and RuntimeSelectionPolicy.

(a) `export function installedExecutable(p: string | undefined, basePath, foldCase = defaultFoldCase)`. Rejections, in order:
- blank: 'node executable not found';
- !path.isAbsolute: 'node executable is not an absolute path';
- unresolvable project: 'the project directory cannot be resolved';
- realpath ENOENT: 'node executable not found'; any other error: 'node executable cannot be resolved';
- not a regular file: 'node executable is not a regular file';
- inside the real project (folded): 'node executable resolves inside the project'.
Otherwise it returns { accepted: real }. Share RF06's installedArtifact checks through one private helper rather than copying them (JetBrains select with no root).

(b) `export function isOutsideProject(p, basePath, foldCase)`. True only when p is absolute and neither path.normalize(p) nor its realpath, if it resolves, isWithin path.resolve(basePath) or the real project. Comparisons use comparablePath and are folded. Any error gives false.

(c) `export function protectedPathEntries(value, basePath, delimiter = path.delimiter)` keeps, as written, the entries whose unquoted form (trimmed, surrounding double quotes removed) isOutsideProject. `export function nodeOnProtectedPath(value, basePath, windows)` returns the first kept entry's path.join(unquoted, windows ? 'node.exe' : 'node') that statSync says isFile. It searches in-process, never by a bare name.

(d) `export function protectedNodeCandidate(env, home, windows, basePath): string | undefined`, mirroring the JetBrains resolveNodeExecutable order:
- MOE_NODE_COMMAND, trimmed and with surrounding quotes stripped;
- on non-Windows with a home, home/.local/share/moe/node/current/bin/node when it is a file and X_OK;
- nodeOnProtectedPath(the PATH value, with the key matched case-insensitively on Windows);
- on Windows, the first existing of ProgramFiles/nodejs/node.exe, ProgramFiles(x86)/nodejs/node.exe, LOCALAPPDATA/Programs/nodejs/node.exe, LOCALAPPDATA/nvm/current/node.exe and APPDATA/nvm/node.exe;
- on non-Windows, the first existing of /opt/homebrew/bin/node, /usr/local/bin/node, home/.nvm/current/bin/node, the name-max dir under home/.nvm/versions/node/*/bin/node, and /usr/bin/node;
- otherwise undefined.
The first candidate found is the one validated. A rejected candidate is refused; the search does not move on to the next one.

(e) `export function protectedDaemonCommand(basePath, root, node)`. It checks the daemon via installedArtifact(root, 'daemon/index.js', basePath) first, then installedExecutable(node, basePath), and returns { refused: reason } on the first rejection. Otherwise it returns { ready: { node: realNode, args: [realDaemon, 'start', '--project', basePath], cwd: path.dirname(realDaemon) } }.

(f) `export function protectedDaemonEnvironment(env, basePath, nodePath, windows, home)` returns a copy:
- NODE_OPTIONS and NODE_PATH are removed (case-insensitively on Windows);
- one PATH spelling is kept (on Windows, the sorted-first key equal to PATH ignoring case; the others are removed);
- its value is protectedPathEntries([dirname(nodePath), ...current entries, ...on non-Windows the existing ~/.local/share/moe/node/current/bin and ~/.local/share/moe/npm/bin].filter(non-blank) deduped, basePath).

(g) startDaemon: right after the startInProgress guard, `if (runtimeProfile(projectPath) === 'protected')` routes to a private startProtectedDaemon(projectPath). That method:
- computes protectedDaemonCommand(projectPath, installedRoot(this.extensionPath), protectedNodeCandidate(process.env, HOME || USERPROFILE, win32, projectPath));
- on refused, logs and calls showErrorMessage with `Protected execution profile: ${reason}. Project and PATH copies of the Moe daemon are not used.` and returns, spawning nothing;
- otherwise spawns with { detached: true, stdio: 'ignore', windowsHide: true, cwd, env }, inside the same startInProgress, error/spawn/unref, waitForDaemonInfo and catch handling as the legacy path.
resolveGlobalConfigDaemonPath and resolveDaemonRuntime are never called under protected. If a private spawn helper is shared, the legacy call keeps exactly its current options keys and messages.

Error handling: every fs failure inside the selection functions becomes a rejection or undefined and nothing throws. Spawn errors keep the legacy catch: a log line plus the ENOENT-aware message. Legacy code paths and bytes are unchanged. Step 1's tests must now pass.
